    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d469">

                <pb facs="0634" n="622" sameAs="frus:frus1946v08/pg622"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 Control (Korea)/1–2546: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Political Adviser in
                        Korea</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Benninghoff</hi>)<anchor n="38"
                        xml:id="d469-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-01-26">January 26, 1946</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>13. The following is full translation of Tass statement on Korean question
                    appearing Soviet press January 25 as received from Embassy Moscow as No. 227,
                    January 25:</p>
                <p>[Here follows quotation of telegram printed on <ref target="#pg617">page
                        617</ref>.]</p>
                <p>Foregoing version of draft proposals and proceedings that led to the Moscow
                    communiqué is substantially correct. In same connection <pb facs="0635" n="623"
                        xml:id="pg623"/> Actg. Secretary at his press conference of 25th made the
                    following statement:</p>
                <p>[Here follows quotation of statement printed in Department of State <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Bulletin</hi>, February 3, 1946, page 155.]</p>
                <p>General Hodge may use the foregoing in any way he sees appropriate to clarify the
                    matter in the minds of the public or persons interested. The American paper
                    referred to by Tass is being communicated to you separately.<anchor n="39"
                        xml:id="d469-f2"/> The agreement on Korea contained in the communiqué is,
                    with two minor alterations, exactly in the form presented by the Russians.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Byrnes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d469-f1" n="38" type="source" xml:id="d469-f1-content">
                <p>This telegram was not received in Seoul until February 9.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d469-f2" n="39" xml:id="d469-f2-content">
                <p>Sent in telegram 15, January 29; see footnote 28, <ref target="#pg617">p.
                        617</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
